```
// Close is allowed only at MAIN, and only after a completed get_workorder lookup
// in this session, within the last hour, showing a GRANTED approval by a HUMAN
// for the same work order at the same site.
@id("close-main-after-human-approval")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"close_workorder", resource)
when { context.input.site_id == "MAIN" }
when temporal {
  formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"get_workorder"::response{
    eventResource: resource,
    input.site_id: context.input.site_id,
    input.wonum: context.input.wonum,
    output.approval_outcome: Drupe::get_workorder_Output_approval_outcome::"GRANTED",
    output.approver_type: Drupe::get_workorder_Output_approver_type::"HUMAN"
  }
};

// Read-only lookups are permitted. get_workorder must be permitted so that its
// response is recorded and can serve as the approval confirmation.
@id("allow-read-only-lookups")
permit (
  principal,
  action in [
    Drupe::Action::"get_workorder",
    Drupe::Action::"authority_get_approval",
    Drupe::Action::"list_workorders",
    Drupe::Action::"get_my_assigned_workorders",
    Drupe::Action::"get_workorder_tasks",
    Drupe::Action::"get_workorder_costs",
    Drupe::Action::"get_workorder_actuals_vs_planned",
    Drupe::Action::"get_workorder_kpis",
    Drupe::Action::"get_schedule_calendar",
    Drupe::Action::"get_failure_codes"
  ],
  resource
);

// The agent must never approve work orders itself, even if another policy is
// added later that would permit it.
@id("never-approve-workorders")
forbid (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"approve_workorder", resource);
```

I used `get_workorder` as the approval check because its output has enum fields (`approval_outcome`, `approver_type`) with known values (GRANTED, HUMAN). `authority_get_approval` returns free-text strings whose accepted values are not in the schema. If your system uses specific strings there, the close policy would need a second policy for that path.

The close policy matches the enum values through their entity form, `Drupe::get_workorder_Output_approval_outcome::"GRANTED"`. I could not confirm that the engine accepts this form in a temporal pattern. If it expects plain string literals, swap them in.
